172e|v|The lungs of an animal or bird; -- sometimes coarsely applied to the lungs of a human being.	o:280a,23,3~280a,23,3
173c|a|Having the same, or nearly the same, appearance, qualities, or characteristics; resembling; similar to; similar; alike; -- often with in and the particulars of the resemblance; as, they are like each other in features, complexion, and many traits of character. ; Equal, or nearly equal; as, fields of like extent. ; Having probability; affording probability; probable; likely. ; Inclined toward; disposed to; as, to feel like taking a walk. ; In a manner like that of; in a manner similar to; as, do not act like him. ; In a like or similar manner. ; Likely; probably. ; To suit; to please; to be agreeable to. ; To be pleased with in a moderate degree; to approve; to take satisfaction in; to enjoy. ; To liken; to compare.	j:req,5,2;txc,4,2~req,5,2;txc,4,2
