173i|a|Worthy of belief; probable; credible; as, a likely story. ; Having probability; having or giving reason to expect; -- followed by the infinitive; as, it is likely to rain. ; Similar; like; alike. ; Such as suits; good-looking; pleasing; agreeable; handsome. ; Having such qualities as make success probable; well adapted to the place; promising; as, a likely young man; a likely servant.	j:hid,64,11;1g0d,44,11;r09,40,20;1txy,33,5;biu,25,25;rhh,19,6;998,16,7;15jo,15,4;amy,12,3;16fq,8,6;bj0,6,2;9fm,5,2;1ppl,3,9;1rgu,0,5~biu,25,25;r09,40,20;hid,64,11;1g0d,44,11;1ppl,3,9;998,16,7;16fq,8,6;rhh,19,6;1txy,33,5;1rgu,0,5;15jo,15,4;amy,12,3;9fm,5,2;bj0,6,2	e:16ri,43,195;1byh,39,715;yn2,26,14;2911,23,134;1p1y,19,30;r9x,15,5;1huf,12,5;ri7,5,3;23ym,3,4~1byh,39,715;16ri,43,195;2911,23,134;1p1y,19,30;yn2,26,14;1huf,12,5;r9x,15,5;23ym,3,4;ri7,5,3
